msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixracer-overview.rst:223
#: 5c69f1c3e29c42c5a2c3fa943435b8ac
msgid "This port has built in inverters on the TX and RX lines and shunt resistors which allow them to be tied together and connected to an FrSky receiver's SPort input for telemetry. It is on by default, and only :ref:`SERIAL4_PROTOCOL<SERIAL4_PROTOCOL>` needs to be set to \"10\" for FrSky passthrough telemetry to be sent to the receiver. See :ref:`common-frsky-telemetry` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixracer-overview.rst:225
#: a431e8f01c944d61a72489eaff8fe420
msgid "The operation of the TX/RX path inverter can be disabled by setting the :ref:`SERIAL4_OPTIONS<SERIAL4_OPTIONS>` parameter to \"2\" to \"invert\" the TX , which will turn off the inversion for both the TX and RX pins. This will allow normal UART operation, if desired."
msgstr ""

